<title>UK: Laura Ashley gains after distribution deal.</title>
<headline>Laura Ashley gains after distribution deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British fashion and furnishings group Laura Ashley Plc gained over four percent on Tuesday after the company said it was taking direct control of its distribution operations.</p>
<p>Laura Ashley shares were up eight pence at 189-1/2p by 1146 GMT while the broader market was slightly weaker. Some 190,000 shares had changed hands by that time.</p>
<p>Laura Ashley said it agreed to take over distribution and logistics from Federal Express in a deal costing around one million stg, including the purchase of fixed assets.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
